# Prodet Platform — Active development conventions

The repository is in active development. Read [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) and [docs/02-architecture/system-overview.md](mdc:docs/02-architecture/system-overview.md) before substantive changes.

## Architecture invariants (do not redesign)

- **One Next.js App Router app.** Public site, admin console, and client portal in the same codebase under `src/app/[locale]/{(public),(auth),(client),admin}`. No microservices.
- **Postgres on Supabase + Drizzle.** Schema in `src/db/schema/`, migrations in `drizzle/migrations/` (forward-only).
- **Three locales.** `fr` (default, complete), `ar` (RTL), `en`. i18n via `next-intl`.
- **Swiver coexistence.** Manual export at MVP, API-driven at Phase 4.
- **AI proposes, humans approve.** No autonomous push to Swiver. No customer chatbot.
- **No public prices, stock, or payment** at MVP.
- **Boring tech bias.** Use the stack in [docs/02-architecture/tech-stack.md](mdc:docs/02-architecture/tech-stack.md). New deps need an ADR.

## Code conventions

- TypeScript **strict**.
- `snake_case` for DB tables/columns; `camelCase` for TS variables; `PascalCase` for types/components.
- Server components by default; mark `'use client'` only when needed.
- Server actions for mutations from the UI; route handlers for webhooks.
- Zod-validate every external input (form, webhook, LLM output).
- Forms via React Hook Form + Zod. No uncontrolled inputs.
- RTL-safe: use Tailwind logical utilities (`ms-*`, `me-*`, `ps-*`, `pe-*`); avoid `ml-*` / `mr-*` outside legacy code.
- Comments explain *why*, not *what*. No narrative comments.
- **No emojis** anywhere — code, copy, commits.
- shadcn/ui copied into `src/components/ui/` (full ownership). Composed components in `src/components/`.

## Mutations and audit

- Every state change writes a row to `audit_log`.
- Service-role Supabase key NEVER ships to the client; only server actions / route handlers.
- RLS enabled on all tables; admin paths use service-role with explicit `assertRole(...)`.

## Workflow

- Run `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm test` before declaring work done.
- Drizzle migrations: forward-only. Generate via `pnpm db:generate`, apply via `pnpm db:migrate`.
- Commit messages follow conventional commits style (`feat(scope): ...`, `fix(scope): ...`, `chore(scope): ...`, `docs(scope): ...`).
- Souhail commits and pushes. Agents may stage when explicitly asked.

## Out of scope (do not add without explicit ask)

- Online payment, public price/stock display, auto-push to Swiver, WhatsApp Business API, OCR, chatbot, blog, AI order intake (until Slice B scoped). See [docs/01-product/non-goals.md](mdc:docs/01-product/non-goals.md).

